From: Mate Molnar <matemolnar88@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pco: predicate only small if bodies

can_pred_exec() turned every non-nested if into predicated code, so large
bodies (GSK's per-corner rounded-rect coverage: pow/log/exp per corner)
ran for every pixel. Keep predication for bodies of up to 8 instructions
and use real branches beyond that. GE8300: GSK UI frame 0.35 -> ~0.25 s,
vkmark desktop 100 -> 140 FPS, output unchanged.
---
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_cf.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_cf.c
@@ -93,11 +93,35 @@
    return last_instr->op == PCO_OP_BR;
 }
 
+/* ponytail: fixed threshold, measured on GE8300 (GSK rounded-corner math).
+ * Predicated bodies run for every lane; past a handful of instructions a
+ * real branch that the whole group can skip is cheaper.
+ */
+#define PCO_PRED_CF_MAX_INSTRS 8U
+
+static inline unsigned body_num_instrs(struct list_head *body)
+{
+   unsigned n = 0;
+
+   if (list_is_empty(body))
+      return 0;
+
+   pco_block *block = pco_cf_node_as_block(pco_cf_node_head(body));
+   pco_foreach_instr_in_block (instr, block)
+      n++;
+
+   return n;
+}
+
 static inline bool can_pred_exec(pco_if *pif)
 {
    if (PCO_DEBUG(NO_PRED_CF))
       return false;
 
+   if (body_num_instrs(&pif->then_body) + body_num_instrs(&pif->else_body) >
+       PCO_PRED_CF_MAX_INSTRS)
+      return false;
+
    /* Skip if there is any nesting. */
    if (list_length(&pif->then_body) > 1 || list_length(&pif->else_body) > 1)
       return false;
